    {
      q: 'Galtung\'s distinction between negative and positive peace separates:',
      choices: ['Wars between and within states', 'Absence of direct violence (negative) from absence of the structural conditions — exploitation, exclusion — that generate it (positive)', 'Peace treaties and truces', 'Cold wars and hot wars'],
      answer: 1,
      why: 'A society can stop shooting (negative peace) while structural violence — blocked opportunity, institutionalised humiliation — keeps generating grievance. Peacebuilding targets the second, which is why it is slower and harder than peacemaking.',
